Am(a,b,c){return"How it works\n\u2022 You bought a car \u2014 you have "+a+" days to register it. You can sell it earlier under a sales contract without registration.\n\u2022 Apply here, the inspection takes place at the traffic police site in the city where the car is (one hour). State fee "+b+", the plates stay.\n\u2022 The inspection checks the VIN and bans \u2014 hidden problems of the car will surface.\n\u2022 Missed the deadline \u2014 fine "+c+" (art. 19.22 of the Code of Administrative Offences).\n\u2022 Changed the details in your passport \u2014 the cars must be registered again."},
gAr(){return"GosBuy"},
gLe(){return"Before buying a car, check its ID in AvtoHistory \u2014 it helps spot registration bans or a re-stamped VIN before you travel to see it."},
gLf(){return"Inspect the car yourself or call a car picker \u2014 the chance of finding a hidden defect is much higher than with a casual look."},
gLg(){return"When haggling by the hood, do not be afraid to name your price \u2014 a refusal from the seller does not always kill the deal, the talks can go on."},
gLh(){return"Keep the car in a garage or in a free yard in your home city \u2014 paid parking in another city charges for every hour."},
gLi(){return"In PlameFinance, a loan taken and repaid right away will not raise your rating faster \u2014 after each closure the pause before the next loan grows."},
gLj(){return"Lower the price gradually: in one step the seller gives up about half the gap between his price and yours, so a sharp drop only annoys him."},
gLk(){return"Seller patience is not endless \u2014 after three clearly rude offers they will close the chat, and you will not be able to return to it."},
gLl(){return"An item from your inventory is a useful trump card in haggling: if the seller accepts it, the lowest price drops by the discount value."},
gLm(){return"Found a hidden defect during the inspection \u2014 show it right in the chat. The seller knows about the problem and will give in more willingly."},
gLn(){return"A car picker costs five percent of the car price, but finds a hidden defect in almost a third of cases \u2014 a self-inspection does this many times less often."},
gLo(){return"The most expensive repair is the engine: it eats a fifth of the car value. Body and gearbox cost fifteen percent, interior and electrics five to seven."},
gLp(){return"A hidden defect does not disappear by itself: a re-stamped VIN or a registration ban will surface on resale and scare off the buyer."},
gLq(){return"Three cars fit into a yard in your home city for free. Anything beyond that goes to paid parking with hourly charges."},
gLr(){return"A garage pays off quickly if you are often in the city: cars stand there for free and are out of reach of vandals."},
gLs(){return"When leaving the city for a long time, move the cars to free spots \u2014 paid parking keeps ticking even when you have forgotten about it."},
gLt(){return"An apartment brings in about five percent of its value per month, a house seven. In expensive cities the rate is even higher."},
gLu(){return"Rented-out housing stops working for you: while tenants live there, it gives no parking spots and does not protect the yard."},
gLv(){return"A long contract pays better but is riskier: after a monthly rental the housing breaks down in about a quarter of cases, after a daily one much less often."},
gLw(){return"There are three game days to repair a major breakdown. Make it in time and tenants pay in full, be late and the income is cut by almost a third."},
gLx(){return"Your own expensive apartment in the city noticeably lowers the risk of vandals scratching a car in the yard."},
gLy(){return"A cheap apartment does a poor job of blocking noise: you wake up before the alarm more often in it."},
gLz(){return"The pause between loans doubles after each closed credit and reaches sixteen days. Take bigger ones, but less often."},
gLA(){return"An overdue payment adds a fine to the debt balance, and then the bailiffs come: they may take half the balance, a car or even housing."},
gLB(){return"Property works as collateral and raises the available credit level, but the starter apartment does not count."},
gLC(){return"Reputation feeds you directly: the higher it is, the more often buyers respond to your listings."},
gLD(){return"A missed meeting costs half a reputation point, and two in a row in one chat close it for good."},
gLE(){return"Do not overprice: if you ask three times the market price, buyers will come five times less often."},
gLF(){return"You can be an hour late to a meeting, after that the deal falls through. If the other side agreed to wait, the margin grows to three hours."},
gLG(){return"A train is the cheapest, a plane is faster but adds two hours for the airport. Your own car costs fuel, but adds mileage."},
gLH(){return"In a city where you have free housing, sleep is free and carries no risk of theft, so you do not need a hotel."},
gLI(){return"A call can reschedule a meeting or ask to unblock a chat, but there is only one attempt per game day."},
gLJ(){return"The signature on the contract is checked against your sample: draw it similarly, or the deal will fall through."},
gLK(){return"Reconnaissance in AvtoHistory is free: first find out whether there is any finding at all, and only then pay for the details."},
